      "id": 1,
      "text": "Horton sits in the northeast corner of Hanover Township, a civil township in Jackson County, Michigan.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hanover_Township%2C_Jackson_County%2C_Michigan"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The community takes its name from Abiel Tripp, the first person to settle in the area that is now Horton.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://99wfmk.com/horton-michigan/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In the late 1800s and early 1900s, Horton boasted a lively mix of hotels, saloons, and band concerts that drew visitors from surrounding farms.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://99wfmk.com/horton-michigan/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Medicine shows in Horton sold so‑called “Indian Medicine,” a herbal concoction made from local plants and extracts.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://99wfmk.com/horton-michigan/"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Roller skating rinks were a popular pastime in Horton, offering a splash of excitement for residents and travelers alike.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://99wfmk.com/horton-michigan/"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Livery stables in Horton provided horse‑drawn transportation, helping the town connect with nearby markets and rail lines.",
